# @facet/turing — the abstract-machine tape altitude.
#
# THE PHYSICAL SUBSTRATE FLOOR of the polyglot cascade. Per Alex
# 2026-07-17 (verbatim, session-crystallizing):
#
#   *"Ground the translation in the physical substrate. If we know
#    what the machine does at the substrate level, the languages on
#    top become flavours. Not categorical new grammar."*
#
#   *"@facet/turing as tape floor."*
#
#   *"@facet/turing/rust as species means Rust IS a lens on the tape."*
#
# @facet/turing IS the abstract-machine tape altitude — the ONE
# altitude at which Church-Turing 1936 grounds every Turing-complete
# language as a specialization over the same physical substrate. The
# tape is the linear-symbol surface of the abstract machine; states
# are the machine's discrete configurations; transitions are the
# per-step deterministic move. Every higher-altitude language
# (@facet/rust, @facet/mirror, @facet/gleam, @facet/wasm, ...) becomes
# a lens on this floor rather than a categorically-new grammar.
#
# === Church-Turing 1936 as substrate authority ===
#
# Reference (per docs/math/polyglot-loss-aware-computational-
# translation.md §3.4 sub-theorem 3.4 universal-hub existence):
# Turing 1936 *"On Computable Numbers, with an Application to the
# Entscheidungsproblem"* (Proc. Lond. Math. Soc. s2-42:230-265) and
# Church 1936 *"An Unsolvable Problem of Elementary Number Theory"*
# (Am. J. Math. 58:345-363). The equivalence establishes: every
# Turing-complete language is inter-simulatable with the tape
# machine model. Hence @facet/turing is a candidate machine-substrate
# hub for any (source_lang, target_lang) polyglot pair.
#
# === substrate-already-had-the-word ===
#
# Per shards/code.mirror docblock: "@facet/llvm, @facet/fortran each
# declare the same five-op block at their altitude." The substrate
# ALREADY named @facet/turing as adjacent-altitude candidate via
# Alex's 2026-07-17 ratification. This shard NAMES what the substrate
# already carries at family-root discipline; MINTS the species-decl
# per Mara canonical spec `1ce68c3` §9.1 M1 forward-promise.
#
# Taut audit `d0572cd` §1.3 grep-verified ABSENT: 0 matches for
# `@facet/turing`, `@facet/assembler`, `@facet/asm`, `turing.tape`,
# `universal.tape`. No substrate-already-had-the-word conflict.
# Small vocabulary (~10-15 species per §9.1); the mint is the FLOOR
# of the cascade chain, not the top.
#
# === composition altitude: FLOOR ===
#
# Every other @facet/X species sits ABOVE this altitude. The typed
# carriers (symbol, state, tape, head_position, transition, program)
# are the substrate the higher-altitude grammars SPECIALIZE via
# their own cascade species. The five-op prism at family-root
# altitude declares the discipline; the typed carriers below declare
# the substrate the discipline COMPOSES OVER.
#
# The dogfood bilateral `turing_well_formed` (per Mara `a0f4d3f`
# bilateral-shape mint) witnesses that a candidate `program` (set
# of transitions + initial state) is a well-formed Turing machine
# — deterministic transition function, halt-state well-defined,
# tape-alphabet finite. This is the substrate-floor admissibility
# check every higher-altitude cascade routes through when it
# discharges to the tape floor.
#
# === spec context ===
#
# docs/specs/polyglot-loss-aware-computational-translation.md §9.1
# M1 (Mara `1ce68c3`, 2026-07-17) — the mint plan forward-promise
# THIS shard discharges. §2.3 (tape as serialization target, not
# master) grounds the altitude framing. §4.1 (concrete instantiation
# chain) names @facet/turing as the middle hub in the Rust →
# LLVM → Turing → mirror loop.
#
# docs/math/polyglot-loss-aware-computational-translation.md §3.4
# (Mara `dc4ad4c`, 2026-07-17) — Church-Turing citation grounding
# universal-hub existence for arbitrary (A, B) pair. §1.1 places
# @facet/turing as one object in the `Cascade_@facet` category.
#
# boot/01-meta.mirror (Taut audit `d0572cd` §1.5) — the universal
# AST parameterized by grammar sits at ADJACENT altitude (boot-
# grammar altitude, above tape floor). The tape-floor grammar is
# the physical-substrate ground; the boot-grammar AST is one
# altitude up (language-agnostic symbolic surface); each `@facet/X`
# is another altitude further up.
#
# === substrate decisions ===
#
# [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]] — this file IS the
# substrate declaration; nothing lives above it as authority for
# what @facet/turing carries.
# [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]] — five-op prism
# discipline at family-root; typed carriers below.
# [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] — the lift is Church-Turing
# 1936 → substrate-decl (not re-derivation).
# [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] — the word already
# lived in the substrate via Alex's ratification; this shard names
# what was implicit.
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] — every action body `\` blocked;
# realisation per-consumer, not pre-committed here.
#
# === related shards ===
#
# shards/code.mirror — family root (@facet discipline).
# shards/code/rust.mirror — sibling species precedent for five-op
# + typed-carrier + build-property surface shape.
# shards/code/wasm.mirror — sibling machine-substrate hub precedent.
# shards/cascade.mirror — the family-root that will target-grammar
# THIS species via `@cascade/code/llvm/turing`,
# `@cascade/code/turing/mirror`, `@cascade/code/rust/turing` per
# Mara §9.2 M2 forward-promise (Reed follow-up domain).
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/code/turing.mirror`
# declares `@facet/turing` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_
# namespace`.

# === typed carriers for the tape substrate ===
#
# Small vocabulary per §9.1 M1: symbol, state, tape, head_position,
# transition, program. The head_move discriminator + halt_condition
# variant admit the deterministic-transition + halt-state
# vocabulary Church-Turing 1936 requires. Every carrier is a
# substrate-typed ref so higher-altitude cascade species can
# construct/consume via @mirror/store OID discipline.

# `symbol` — one cell's contents on the tape. Substrate-typed ref
# so the tape-alphabet is species-configurable per cascade (LLVM IR
# → tape uses byte-typed symbols; mirror-composition → tape uses
# OID-typed symbols). The tape-alphabet finiteness is a
# well-formedness obligation on `program`, not a floor constraint.
type symbol = ref

# `state` — one discrete machine configuration. Substrate-typed ref
# so states can carry per-species metadata (basic-block index for
# LLVM cascade, node OID for mirror cascade, byte-offset for raw
# assembly cascade). The state-set finiteness is a
# well-formedness obligation on `program`.
type state = ref

# `tape` — the linear-symbol surface. A sequence of symbols;
# unbounded to either side per Turing 1936 (the finite-tape
# constraint is a per-cascade admissibility choice, not a
# floor constraint). Each cascade species may add its own
# tape-length bound via loss-lens.
type tape = [symbol]

# `head_position` — offset into tape. Signed integer so unbounded-
# to-either-side tape has natural representation (0 = initial;
# negative = extended-left; positive = extended-right). The
# tape-position discipline (linear or content-addressed) is a
# cascade-species choice per §4.4 (mirror-cascade reifies positions
# as edge-labels since mirror altitude has no linear addresses).
type head_position = ref

# `head_move` — discriminator on transition's head-motion field.
# Three variants per Turing 1936: left one cell, right one cell,
# stay. The stay variant is admitted because higher-altitude
# languages (LLVM SSA, mirror composition) have branches that
# don't advance the tape — the cascade species may erase stays
# in its loss-lens if the target grammar is strict-move only.
type head_move = move_left | move_right | move_stay

# `transition` — one rule of the transition function. Per
# Turing 1936 δ : (state, symbol) → (state, symbol, head_move).
# Deterministic: at most one transition per (state, symbol) pair;
# non-determinism is enforced-absent by `turing_well_formed`.
type transition = {
  from_state: state,
  read_symbol: symbol,
  to_state: state,
  write_symbol: symbol,
  move: head_move,
}

# `program` — the full Turing machine. Transitions + initial state
# + halt-state set. Non-deterministic programs are ill-formed
# (bilateral `turing_well_formed` rejects). Finite-state and
# finite-alphabet constraints admitted at construction time via
# the substrate's typed-carrier discipline; enforced at
# `turing_well_formed` discharge.
type program = {
  transitions: [transition],
  initial_state: state,
  halt_states: [state],
}

# `configuration` — a machine at one instant. State + tape + head.
# The dynamic runtime object per cascade species'
# `apply_transition` action; snapshotted at each step. Used by
# higher-altitude cascades to reason about intermediate
# computations (e.g., @cascade/code/turing/mirror reifies each
# configuration as one substrate-composition node).
type configuration = {
  current_state: state,
  tape: tape,
  head: head_position,
}

# `verdict_kind` — discriminator on halt_check output. Distinguishes
# halted (in halt_states), running (not yet halted), or ill-formed
# (state not in program's state-set). Higher-altitude cascades
# use this to route their own halt-witnessing per their loss-lens.
type verdict_kind = halted | running | ill_formed

# === actions on the tape substrate ===
#
# All actions `\` obligation-blocked per [[feedback-craft-not-
# deliver]]. The discipline is declared HERE; the realisation per
# cascade species (@cascade/code/A/turing, @cascade/code/turing/B)
# provides the actual byte-level implementation. Each action's
# signature is the CONTRACT the cascade must honor.

# `read` — byte-level tape read. Returns the symbol at head_position
# on tape. Pure function on (tape, head_position). Extension
# semantics: reading beyond tape bounds returns the tape-alphabet's
# blank symbol per cascade species' convention (blank is not a
# floor primitive; it's a species choice at construction time).
read(t: tape, h: head_position) -> symbol { \ }

# `write` — byte-level tape write. Returns a NEW tape with the
# symbol at head_position replaced. Pure function on (tape,
# head_position, symbol). Tapes are immutable at substrate
# altitude; mutation is realized at @io boundary by cascade
# species (LLVM cascade uses register writes; mirror cascade
# creates new content-addressed nodes).
write(t: tape, h: head_position, s: symbol) -> tape { \ }

# `move_left` — decrement head_position by one cell. Pure.
# Unbounded-left tape admitted; the position may become negative.
# Each cascade species' loss-lens may bound the tape and surface
# left-underflow as loss.
move_left(h: head_position) -> head_position { \ }

# `move_right` — increment head_position by one cell. Pure. Same
# unbounded-right admission as `move_left`.
move_right(h: head_position) -> head_position { \ }

# `apply_transition` — one step of the machine. Reads the current
# symbol at head, matches against program's transition-set,
# applies the write + move, transitions the state. Returns the
# new configuration. Pure function on (program, configuration);
# realisation per cascade species reads its concrete transition
# encoding (LLVM basic-block dispatch, mirror graph traversal).
apply_transition(p: program, c: configuration) -> configuration { \ }

# `halt_check` — bilateral predicate: is this configuration halted?
# Discriminator over verdict_kind. Higher-altitude cascades use
# this to witness computation termination per their own loss-lens
# — cascade may report `halted` as loss=0, `running` as
# loss=continuation-cost, `ill_formed` as loss=unbounded per §5
# admissibility discipline.
halt_check(p: program, c: configuration) -> verdict_kind { \ }

# `equivalent` — bilateral predicate: do two programs compute the
# same function? UNDECIDABLE in general per Rice's theorem (per
# docs/math/epistemologic/pact/bilateral-sentinel.md §Rice-safety);
# realisation per cascade species is APPROXIMATE — cascade may
# discharge via structural bisimulation (Milner 1989), trace
# equivalence up to bounded fuel, or bytecode-hash-equality per
# its loss-lens choice. The verdict shape is universal; the
# per-cascade approximation is species-local. Content-addressed
# check per Mara `701828a` §1 remains Rice-safe.
equivalent(p1: program, p2: program) -> verdict { \ }

# === dogfood bilateral (per Mara `a0f4d3f` shape mint) ===
#
# Multi-line format per Reed remediation `1ad8bb5` — single-line
# `bilateral X { sentinel "..." arity N }` is SKIPPED by the corpus
# loader. Every bilateral below uses the multi-line block.
#
# `turing_well_formed` witnesses that `program` is a valid Turing
# machine per Turing 1936:
#   - transition function is DETERMINISTIC (at most one transition
#     per (state, symbol) pair)
#   - halt_states ⊆ state-set (every halt state is reachable via
#     transitions or IS the initial state)
#   - alphabet is finite (implicit via substrate-typed refs; the
#     bilateral's byte-composite sentinel enforces the check)
#   - state-set is finite (same discipline as alphabet)
#
# Sentinel `tape=well-formed-machine-state` per the substrate's
# canonical form: content-addressed byte-check on the program's
# structural OID vs the well-formed-Turing-machine invariants.
# Rice-safe per Mara `701828a` §1 byte-containment discipline
# (structural check on program OID; no semantic introspection).

bilateral turing_well_formed {
  sentinel "tape=well-formed-machine-state"
  arity 1
}
turing_well_formed(p: program) -> verdict { \ }

# `turing_halts_on` — bilateral predicate: does program p halt when
# started on tape t at initial state? UNDECIDABLE in general per
# Halting Problem (Turing 1936). Realisation per cascade species
# is APPROXIMATE — bounded-fuel simulation, structural termination
# analysis, or explicit annotation per species' loss-lens.
# Sentinel names the substrate-floor structural invariant checked
# at discharge; Rice-safety per Mara `701828a` (the CHECK is
# content-addressed even if the underlying question is undecidable
# — the bilateral discharges IFF the sentinel matches; sentinel
# match is byte-level containment).

bilateral turing_halts_on {
  sentinel "computation=halts-under-fuel-bound"
  arity 2
}
turing_halts_on(p: program, t: tape) -> verdict { \ }

# `configuration_reachable` — bilateral predicate: is configuration
# `c` reachable from program p's initial configuration via zero or
# more applications of apply_transition? Substrate-floor reachability
# check used by higher-altitude cascades to witness intermediate
# computation state (e.g., @cascade/code/mirror/turing reifies each
# reachable configuration as a substrate-composition node).
# Sentinel: reachability-under-transitive-closure content-check.
# Rice-safe under bounded-fuel realisation per Mara `701828a`.

bilateral configuration_reachable {
  sentinel "reachability=transitive-closure-under-fuel"
  arity 2
}
configuration_reachable(p: program, c: configuration) -> verdict { \ }

# === outbound declarations ===

out @facet/turing
out symbol
out state
out tape
out head_position
out head_move
out transition
out program
out configuration
out verdict_kind
out read
out write
out move_left
out move_right
out apply_transition
out halt_check
out equivalent
out turing_well_formed
out turing_halts_on
out configuration_reachable
